<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Planning & Scheduling</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Convert organizational demand into feasible production orders with a high-standard 
            planning engine that synchronizes materials, capacity, and lead times.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Master Production Scheduling (MPS)</h2>
        <p>
            Build your factory's forward commitments through a robust Master Production 
            Schedule. Aggregate demand from firm sales orders, contractual commitments, 
            and statistical forecasts into a unified production target. The MPS 
            balancing engine identifies demand spikes and identifies potential 
            capacity shortfalls early, allowing leadership to adjust shifts, 
            outsource labor, or communicate adjusted delivery timelines to 
            customers with factual clarity.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Material Requirements Planning (MRP)</h2>
        <p>
            Drive procurement through algorithmic precision. The MRP engine explodes the 
            Bill of Materials for every scheduled production order, identifying exactly 
            what raw materials need to be bought—and when—to ensure zero-delay 
            production. By factoring in supplier lead times, current safety stock 
             levels, and pending purchase orders, the system generates targeted 
            replenishment alerts that minimize excess inventory while guaranteeing 
            production continuity.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Finite Capacity & Conflict Detection</h2>
        <p>
            Ensure your schedules are executable on the shop floor. The system maintains an 
            accurate model of machine and work center capacity across all shifts. 
            Automated conflict detection identify double-booked assets or labor 
            bottlenecks instantly during the scheduling process. What-if simulation 
            tools allow planners to evaluate the impact of rush orders or machine 
            downtime on the entire production queue, facilitating agile and 
            resilient scheduling.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

